                <pb facs="1008" n="974" xml:id="pg974"/>

                <head>No. 431<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1954-02-06">February 6, 1954</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>According to the United States Delegation Order of the Day (USDEL(OD) 14,
                    February 6, 1954, CFM files, lot M 88, box 168) MacArthur, Merchant, Nash,
                    Bohlen, Bowie, Freund, Davis, Rutter, and Manfull met at 9:45 a.m. in Secretary
                    Dulles’ office to discuss Austria. No record of this meeting has been found in
                    Department of State files.</p>
                <p>According to the same Order of the Day, Secretary Dulles met in his office with
                    Federal Minister of Justice Dehler at 10:30 a.m. No record of this meeting has
                    been found in Department of State files.</p>
                <p>This Order of the Day also states that there would be no United States Delegation
                    meeting on February 6.</p>
            </div>
